---
code: K0029
title: When With Else
severity: ERROR
since: 0.1.0
category: parse
deprecated: False
tags: [parse, syntax, control-flow, when, if, else]
description: "'when' expression cannot have an 'else' branch"
---

A `when` expression evaluates its block when the condition is `true` and implicitly evaluates to `None` when the condition is `false`. Because its fallback is always `None`, `when` does not accept an `else` branch.

## Example

This error occurs when an `else` clause is attached to a `when` expression:

```kura
fn badge(unread: Int) =>
  when unread > 0 {
    #text("{unread}")
  } else {
    #text("0")
  }
```

## Solution

Use `if ... else` when you need an explicit fallback branch, or remove the `else` block if `None` is the desired fallback:

```kura
fn badge(unread: Int) =>
  if unread > 0 {
    #text("{unread}")
  } else {
    #text("0")
  }

fn optional-badge(unread: Int) =>
  when unread > 0 {
    #text("{unread}")
  }
```
